Process technology
ST-T1024 does not inherently require a leading-edge process.
A mature semiconductor process may be attractive because the architecture is intended for:
low computational complexity;
embedded operation;
deterministic timing;
modest memory requirements;
potentially long product lifetimes;
cost-sensitive deployments.
A suitable node—65 nm, 90 nm, 130 nm, 180 nm, or another available process—should therefore be selected after actual area, frequency, power, memory, IP, foundry, packaging, and cost requirements are established.
The process node is an engineering decision, not a fixed requirement of the standard.


